 ## Overview
-3D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization is a differentiable rendering technique that represents a scene as a collection of anisotropic 3D Gaussians and projects them to 2D screen space for real-time image synthesis [S1][S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high-fidelity view synthesis by replacing triangle-based rasterization with Gaussian splatting, enabling gradients to flow back to primitive parameters for optimization [S4, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that may use CPU sorting or software-only pipelines, this method typically relies on GPU-accelerated tile-based rasterization with efficient depth sorting to handle millions of primitives [S4, unofficial].
+3D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization is a screen-space rendering method that projects a set of 3D Gaussian primitives onto a 2D image plane and accumulates color per pixel using alpha compositing [S1][S3, S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of real-time, photorealistic rendering of scenes represented by anisotropic Gaussians, serving as the core differentiable kernel for training and inference [S3, S4, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from triangle-based rasterization by using Gaussian kernels for smooth, aliasing-resistant blending, and from ray-tracing methods by operating directly in screen space with tile-based acceleration [S4, S6, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-*   `means_3D`: $N \times 3$ tensor of Gaussian mean positions in world space.
-*   `quats`: $N \times 4$ tensor of unit quaternions $(w, x, y, z)$ representing rotation.
-*   `scales`: $N \times 3$ tensor of scaling factors $(s_x, s_y, s_z)$.
-*   `opacities`: $N$ tensor of scalar opacity values $\alpha$.
-*   `colors`: $N \times D$ tensor of color coefficients. If `sh_degree` is None, this is $N \times 3$ (RGB). If `sh_degree` > 0, this contains SH coefficients.
-*   `viewmats`: $C \times 4 \times 4$ camera extrinsic matrices $V$.
-*   `Ks`: $C \times 3 \times 3$ camera intrinsic matrices.
-*   `width`, `height`: Image dimensions.
-*   `tile_size`: Integer, default 16. Side length of rasterization tiles.
-*   `near_plane`, `far_plane`: Floats, default 0.01 and 1e10. Clipping distances.
-*   `sh_degree`: Integer or None. Enables spherical harmonics if not None.
-*   `render_mode`: String, e.g., "RGB", "D", "ED", "RGB+D", "RGB+ED".
-*   `rasterize_mode`: String, "classic" or "antialiased".
-*   `camera_model`: String, "pinhole", "ortho", or "fisheye".
-*   `backgrounds`: $C \times 3$ tensor for background color.
