 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [3D Gaussian Splatting Differentiable Rasterizer](2813-3d-gaussian-splatting-differentiable-rasterizer.md)
-The 3D Gaussian Splatting Differentiable Rasterizer is a rendering method that projects 3D Gaussian primitives to 2D screen space and accumulates color per pixel using alpha compositing, enabling gradients to flow back to Gaussian parameters (position, scale, rotation, opacity, color) and camera poses. It differs from its siblings by providing a fully differentiable forward and backward pass that supports optimization of both scene geometry and camera view matrices $P=[R|t]$, unlike the original 3DGS implementation which did not support pose optimization. It builds on [3D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization](2812-3d-gaussian-splatting-rasterization.md) by implementing the specific accumulation and gradient computation logic required for training.
